Small genomes for a local sanity check of the Python VARUS (v2). Do not use
them for benchmarks: an unusually high share of the Schizosaccharomyces pombe
runs in SRA fails the quality gate. species.txt lists both species with their
genome files, for wrappers that loop over several species.

Prerequisites: pip install -e ".[align,logan]" in the repository root plus
hisat2, samtools and fastq-dump on PATH (see README.md, "Installation").

    cd example
    varus runlist "Saccharomyces cerevisiae" --outdir Sc/ --email you@host
    varus index   S.cerevisiae.genome.fa --outdir Sc/genome/ --threads 4
    varus run     "Saccharomyces cerevisiae" S.cerevisiae.genome.fa \
                  --runlist Sc/Runlist.tsv --index Sc/genome/hisatidx \
                  --outdir Sc/ --threads 4 --max-batches 10

Sc/ then contains VARUS.bam (spliced read alignments of all batches),
introns.gff, Coverage.csv, RunStatistics.csv and BatchTimings.tsv. Ten
batches take a few minutes; the optional Logan pre-screen (varus logan) is
described in README.md.

The v1 C++/Perl VARUS (runVARUS.pl, VARUSparameters.txt) lives in the
upstream Gaius-Augustus/VARUS repository.
